      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cambria was founded when John McDermid built a sawmill in 1865, turning a forest of lakes into a growing settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.hillsdalehistoricalsociety.org/cambria-mi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community was named Cambria after Cambria, New York, the hometown of many early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambria%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cambria Mills was platted in 1878 but never incorporated, yet once boasted shops, a hotel, a planing mill, and a large brick school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
